llions:7+8=15. 5, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:1+9=10 +1=11. 1, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:4+3=7 +1=8.\n\nSo the total is 8,154,129,33? Wait, maybe the commas are misplaced. Let me separate the digits:\n\nThe result digits from right to left:\n\nOnes:3.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nTen millions:1.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nWait, but arranging them from left to right (hundred millions to ones):\n\n8 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 3 (ones). \n\nSo that's 815,412,933. Wait, but let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in parts. Let's see:\n\nFirst, add the two numbers: 417,264,422 + 398,148,511.\n\nLet me split them into millions and the rest.\n\n417,264,422 can be written as 417,000,000 + 264,422.\n\n398,148,511 as 398,000,000 + 148,511.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 417,000,000 + 398,000,000 = 815,000,000.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 264,422 + 148,511.\n\n264,422 + 148,511:\n\n264,422 + 100,000 = 364,422.\n\n364,422 + 48,511 = 412,933.\n\nSo total is 815,000,000 + 412,933 = 815,412,933.\n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So that gives me more confidence.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using approximate values to see if it's reasonable.\n\n417 million plus 398 million is roughly 815 million, so the exact total should be 815 million plus the sum of the remaining parts, which are 264,422 and 148,511. Adding those gives about 412,000, so total is around 815.4 million. That seems to fit.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use calculator-like step-by-step:\n\nLet me write down the numbers without commas for clarity:\n\n417264422\n\n+398148511\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n2 +1 =3.\n\nNext digit: 2 +1=3.\n\nNext:4+5=9.\n\nNext:4+8=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nNext digit (ten thousands place):6+4=10, plus 1 is 11.