gits to the left, this 14 would be written as 4 in the hundred millions place and carryover 1 to a new billion place (10th digit).\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nDigits:.\n\nOnes:3.\n\nTens:0.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nMillions:2.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nHundred millions:4 (from 14) with a carryover 1 to the billions place.\n\nSo the billions place is 1. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
