r. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nOnes place: 6 + 4 = 10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 9 + 3 + 1 = 13 → 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 0 + 3 + 1 = 4 → 4, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 1 + 1 = 2 → 2.\n\nTen thousands: 6 + 3 = 9 → 9.\n\nHundred thousands: 6 + 8 = 14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\nMillions: 7 + 7 + 1 = 15 → 5, carryover 1.\n\nTen millions: 7 + 8 + 1 = 16 → 6, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions: 1 + 3 + 1 = 5 → 5.\n\nWait, so the digits from right to left are:.\n\n0 (ones), 3 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 2 (thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 4 (hundred thousands), 5 (millions), 6 (ten millions), 5 (hundred millions). So putting them in order from highest to lowest place:.\n\n5 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
