irst number has 8, second has 6. So 8 +6 =14 plus any carryover?.\n\nWait, let me retrace step by step with correct digit positions:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n1. Units: 5 +6 =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\n2. Tens:1 (from first) +6 (from second) =7 +1 (carryover) =8. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\n3. Hundreds:5 +5 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\n4. Thousands:0 +6 =6 +1 (carryover) =7. Write 7, carryover 0.\n\n5. Ten thousands:8 +2 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:7 +9 =16 +1 (carryover) =17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\n7. Millions:8 (first number) +6 (second number) =14 +1 (carryover)=15. So write 5, carryover 1.\n\n8. Ten millions:3 (first) +5 (second) =8 +1 (carryover) =9. Write 9, carryover 0.\n\n9. Hundred millions:2 (first) +6 (second) =8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nPutting all together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits we've written are:.\n\nUnits:1.\n\nTens:8.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nHundred thousands:7.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nTen millions:9.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nSo the total number is 895,707,078? Wait, let me check the placement again.\n\nWait, the digits from left to right (hundred millions down to units):.\n\nHundred millions place is 8,.\n\nten millions place is 9,.\n\nmillions place is5,.\n\nhundred thousands is7,.\n\nten thousands is0,.\n\nthousands is7,.\n\nhundreds is0,.\n\ntens is8,.\n\nunits is1.\n\nWait that would be 8 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions),5 (millions),7 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),0 (hundreds),8 (tens),1 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
