Second number: 1.\n4 + 1 = 5, plus the carried 1 is 6. Write down 6, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:.\nFirst number:7.\nSecond number:0.\n7 + 0 =7. Write down 7, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:.\nFirst number:8.\nSecond number:3.\n8 +3=11. Write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\nFirst number:1.\nSecond number:1.\n1 +1=2, plus the carried over 1 makes 3. Write down 3, no carryover.\n\nMillions place:.\nFirst number:3.\nSecond number:6.\n3 +6=9. Write down 9, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place:.\nFirst number:8.\nSecond number:0.\n8 +0=8. Write down 8, no carryover.\n\nHundred millions place:.\nFirst number:8.\nSecond number:1.\n8 +1=9. Write down 9, no carryover.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nStarting from the ones digit we had 5, then 1, 6, 7, 1 (from ten thousands place after carryover?), wait, let me retrace.\n\nWait, let me list each digit position's result:.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTens:1.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:1 (with a carryover of 1 to the next higher place).\n\nWait, actually, when we did the ten thousands place, we had 8 +3 =11 plus carryover? Wait no, the carryover was from the previous addition (the thousands place didn't have a carryover, so the ten thousands place was 8+3=11, so that's 1 in the ten thousands place and carryover 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nWait, so the digits from right to left (positions 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition 1 (Ones):5.\n\nPosition 2 (Tens):1 (from 8+2+1=11, so 1 in tens place, carryover 1 to hundreds).\n\nWait, actually, let me re-express the digits step by step properly:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position 1):.\n\nPosition 1 (Ones):.\n\n7 + 8 =15 → 5, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (Tens):.\n\n8 + 2 =10, plus carryover 1 → 11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 3 (Hundreds):.\n\n4 +1 =5, plus carryover 1 →6, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 4 (Thousands):.\n\n7 +0 =7, plus 0 →7.\n\nPosition 5 (Ten thousands):.\n\n8 +3 =11, plus 0 →11 →1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 6 (Hundred thousands):.\n\n1 +1 =2, plus carryover 1 →3, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 7 (Millions):.\n\n3 +6 =9, plus 0 →9.\n\nPosition 8 (Ten millions):.\n\n8 +0 =8, plus 0 →8.\n\nPosition 9 (Hundred millions):.\n\n8 +1 =9, plus 0 →9.\n\nSo the resulting digits from position 1 to 9 (right to left) are:.\n\n5 (ones), 1 (tens), 6 (hundreds),7 (thousands),1 (ten thousands),3 (hundred thousands),9 (millions),8 (ten millions),9 (hundred millions).\n\nTherefore, arranging them from highest to lowest place value (left to right):.\n\n9 (hundred millions),8 (ten millions),9 (millions),3 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),6 (hundreds),1 (tens),5 (ones).\n\nWait, let me check that again:.\n\nWait, the positions are:.\n\nPosition 9: Hundred millions: 9.\n\nPosition 8: Ten millions:8.\n\nPosition7: Millions:9.\n\nPosition6: Hundred thousands:3.\n\nPosition5: Ten thousands:1.\n\nPosition4: Thousands:7.\n\nPosition3: Hundreds:6.\n\nPosition2: Tens:1.\n\nPosition1: Ones:5.\n\nSo putting them together, the number is:.\n\n9 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 5 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
