git 7: 6 (hundreds).\n\nDigit 8: 9 (tens).\n\nDigit 9: 1 (ones).\n\nAlright, so adding them digit by digit from right to left (starting from ones place):.\n\nStarting with Ones place:.\n\nFirst number: 5.\n\nSecond number:1.\n\nSum:5 +1=6. Write down 6. No carry-over.\n\nTens place:.\n\nFirst number:6.\n\nSecond number:9.\n\n6 +9=15. Write down 5, carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\n\nFirst number:4.\n\nSecond number:6.\n\n4 +6=10, plus carryover 1 is 11. Write 1, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place:.\n\nFirst number:1.\n\nSecond number:8.\n\n1 +8=9, plus 1 is 10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n\nFirst number:5.\n\nSecond number:9.\n\n5 +9=14, plus 1 is 15. Write 5, carry over 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n\nFirst number:7.\n\nSecond number:7.\n\n7 +7=14, plus 1 is 15. Write 5, carry over 1.\n\nMillions place:.\n\nFirst number:0.\n\nSecond number:5.\n\n0 +5=5, plus 1 is 6. Write 6, no carry-over.\n\nTen millions place:.\n\nFirst number:4.\n\nSecond number:4.\n\n4 +4=8. Write 8, no carry-over.\n\nHundred millions place:.\n\nFirst number:4.\n\nSecond number:7.\n\n4 +7=11. Write 1, carry over 1.\n\nWait, but since we are at the highest digit (hundred millions), the carry-over 1 would go to the next place, which is billions. So we have to add that 1 as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the ones digit, moving left, the digits we have written are:.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nThousands:0.\n\nTen thousands:5.\n\nHundred thousands:5.\n\nMillions:6.\n\nTen millions:8.\n\nHundred millions:1 (from 4+7=11, so 1 is written here, but actually, the 11 would make the hundred millions place 1 and carry over to billions).\n\nWait, hold on. Let me retrace.\n\nWait, when we added the hundred millions place (digit 1):.\n\nFirst number's hundred millions digit:4.\n\nSecond number's hundred millions digit:7.\n\n4+7=11. So we write 1 in the hundred millions place and carry over 1 to the billions place. Since there ar