rryover.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\n\n4 (first) +9 (second) =13. Write 3, carryover1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\n8 (first) +2 (second) =10, plus carryover1=11. Write 1, carryover1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\n6 (first) +3 (second) =9, plus carryover1=10. Write 0, carryover1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\n0 (first) +3 (second) =3, plus carryover1=4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\n2 (first) +7 (second)=9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\n6 (first) +9 (second)=15. Write 5, carryover1.\n\nWait, but there are no more digits beyond position9, so that carryover1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nPosition1:5.\n\nPosition2:0.\n\nPosition3:9.\n\nPosition4:3.\n\nPosition5:1.\n\nPosition6:0.\n\nPosition7:4.\n\nPosition8:9.\n\nPosition9:5 (from 6+9=15, but with carryover1?).\n\nWait, hold on, let me re-express all the steps again step by step.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones place: 0 +5 =5. Write 5. Carryover 0.\n\n2. Tens place:7 +3 =10. Write 0. Carryover 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:3 +5 =8, plus carryover 1 → 9. Write 9. Carryover 0.\n\n4. Thousands place:4 +9 =13. Write 3. Carryover 1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:8 +2 =10, plus carryover1 →11. Write 1. Carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:6 +3 =9, plus carryover1 →10. Write 0. Carryover1.\n\n7. Millions place:0 +3 =3, plus carryover1 →4. Write4. Carryover0.\n\n8. Ten millions place:2 +7 =9. Write9. Carryover0.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:6 +9 =15. Write5. Carryover1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover1 after the hundred millions place, we need to add a new digit at the beginning (billions place). So the total becomes 1 followed by the digits we've written.\n\nPutting all the digits together from highest to lowest:.\n\nCarryover1 (billions place) then the digits from position9 to 1:.\n\nWait, let's list all the digits we have written in each position:.\n\nPositi