.\n\n          1 1 5 6 3 3 6 5 4.\n        + 9 0 9 7 5 7 3 2 8.\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 4 + 8 = 12. 2, carry 1.\n\nTens: 5 + 2 = 7 + 1 = 8. 8, no carry.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 3 = 9. 9, no carry.\n\nThousands: 3 + 7 = 10. 0, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands: 3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9. 9, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands: 6 + 7 = 13. 3, carry 1.\n\nMillions: 5 + 9 = 14 +1 =15. 5, carry 1.\n\nTen millions: 1 + 0 =1 +1=2. 2, no carry.\n\nHundred millions: 1 +9=10. 0, carry 1.\n\nWait, but the hundred millions place: first number has 1, second has 9. So 1 +9 =10, so we write 0 and carry over 1 to the next column, which is the billions place. Since there are no more digits, that carried 1 becomes a 1 at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:2, Tens:8, Hundreds:9, Thousands:0, Ten thousands:9, Hundred thousands:3, Millions:5, Ten millions:2, Hundred millions:0, and the carried 1 in the billions place. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
