hundred thousands).\n- 0 (ten thousands).\n- 0 (thousands).\n- 4 (hundreds).\n- 6 (tens).\n- 6 (units).\n\nSecond number: 651,850,945.\nBreaking it down:.\n- 6 (hundred millions).\n- 5 (ten millions).\n- 1 (millions).\n- 8 (hundred thousands).\n- 5 (ten thousands).\n- 0 (thousands).\n- 9 (hundreds).\n- 4 (tens).\n- 5 (units).\n\nSo when aligning:.\n\nLet's write them out digit by digit:.\n\nFirst number:.\n7 5 0 8 0 0 4 6 6.\n\nSecond number:.\n6 5 1 8 5 0 9 4 5.\n\nWait, but the second number is 651,850,945, which is 9 digits: 6 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 5 (units). .\n\nFirst number is 750,800,466 which is also 9 digits: 7 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (units).\n\nSo when adding, align each digit:.\n\nStarting from the right (units):.\n\nFirst digit: 6 +5 =11, as before.\n\nSecond digit (tens): 6 +4 =10, plus carryover 1 makes 11.\n\nThird digit (hundreds):4 +9 =13, plus carryover 1 =14. Wait, wait a second! Wait, I think I made a mistake earlier. Let me go step by step again carefully.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nLet me write each number digit by digit with commas to help:.\n\nFirst number: 7 5 0 8 0 0 4 6 6.\n\nSecond number:6 5 1 8 5 0 9 4 5.\n\nWait actually, the positions might be better written as:.\n\nLet me list each digit position from right to left (units to higher places):.\n\nFirst number (750800466):.\n\nPosition 1 (units):6.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):6.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):4.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):0.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):0.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):8.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):0.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):5.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):7.\n\nSecond number (651850945):.\n\nPosition 1 (units):5.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):4.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):9.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):0.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):5.\n\nPosition 6 (