ds:5.\n\nTens:9.\n\nUnits:1.\n\nSo digit positions from right (units) to left (hundred millions):.\n\nPosition1:1 (units).\n\nPosition2:9 (tens).\n\nPosition3:5 (hundreds).\n\nPosition4:0 (thousands).\n\nPosition5:6 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition6:7 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition7:6 (millions).\n\nPosition8:2 (ten millions).\n\nPosition9:8 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, so in the hundred thousands place it's 7, millions is 6? Wait, let me confirm:.\n\nBreaking down 826,760,591:.\n\n- The digits are:.\n\nFrom left to right:.\n\n8 (hundred millions).\n\n2 (ten millions).\n\n6 (millions).\n\n7 (hundred thousands).\n\n6 (ten thousands).\n\n0 (thousands).\n\n5 (hundreds).\n\n9 (tens).\n\n1 (units).\n\nYes, that's right. So the digits in each place are as above.\n\nTherefore, when adding to the first number, which is 347,891,063:.\n\nDigits of first number (347,891,063):.\n\nFrom left to right:.\n\n3 (hundred millions).\n\n4 (ten millions).\n\n7 (millions).\n\n8 (hundred thousands).\n\n9 (ten thousands).\n\n1 (thousands).\n\n0 (hundreds).\n\n6 (tens).\n\n3 (units).\n\nWait, let me confirm:.\n\n347,891,063:.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\n3 (hundred millions).\n\n4 (ten millions).\n\n7 (millions).\n\n8 (hundred thousands).\n\n9 (ten thousands).\n\n1 (thousands).\n\n0 (hundreds).\n\n6 (tens).\n\n3 (units).\n\nYes, so when written digit by digit from right (units) to left (hundred millions):.\n\nPosition1 (units):3.\n\nPosition2 (tens):6.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):0.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):8.\n\nPosition7 (millions):7.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):4.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3.\n\nOkay, so now let's align both numbers digit by digit from right (units) to left (hundred millions):.\n\nFirst number (347891063):.\n\nPositions 1-9:.\n\n1:3.\n\n2:6.\n\n3:0.\n\n4:1.\n\n5:9.\n\n6:8.\n\n7:7.\n\n8:4.\n\n9:3.\n\nSecond number (826760591):.\n\nPositions1-9:.\n\n1:1.\n\n2:9.\n\n3:5.\n\n4:0.\n\n5:6.\n\n6:7.\n\n7:6.\n\n8:2.\n\n