o the next (ten billions) place. But since both numbers don't have a digit beyond the billions, that carried over 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 1.\n\nTens: 6.\n\nHundreds: 3 (with a carryover).\n\nThousands: 2.\n\nTen thousands: 0 (with carryover).\n\nHundred thousands: 5.\n\nMillions: 9.\n\nTen millions: 8.\n\nHundred millions: 3.\n\nBillions: 3 (with a carryover of 1 to the ten billions place).\n\nSo the carried over 1 from the billions addition becomes the ten billions digit. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
