igits properly. Let me list out each digit's place step by step.\n\nLet me write each number with their place values:.\n\nFirst number: 863,636,349.\nBreaking it down:.\n- 8 (hundred millions).\n- 6 (ten millions).\n- 3 (millions).\n- 6 (hundred thousands).\n- 3 (ten thousands).\n- 6 (thousands).\n- 3 (hundreds).\n- 4 (tens).\n- 9 (units).\n\nSecond number: 637,729,581.\nBreaking it down:.\n- 6 (hundred millions).\n- 3 (ten millions).\n- 7 (millions).\n- 7 (hundred thousands).\n- 2 (ten thousands).\n- 9 (thousands).\n- 5 (hundreds).\n- 8 (tens).\n- 1 (units).\n\nNow, adding each corresponding place from right to left (units to hundred millions):.\n\nStarting with units:.\n9 (first) + 1 (second) = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:.\n4 + 8 = 12 + 1 (carry) = 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\n3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9. Write 9, carryover 0.\n\nThousands place:.\n6 (first) + 9 (second) = 15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n3 (first) + 2 (second) = 5 + 1 (carry) = 6. Write 6, carryover 0.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n6 (first) +7 (second) =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place:.\n3 (first) +7 (second)=10 +1 (carry)=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen millions place:.\n6 (first) +3 (second)=9 +1 (carry)=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions place:.\n8 (first) +6 (second)=14 +1 (carry)=15. So write 5 and carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, that carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nUnits:0, Tens:3, Hundreds:9, Thousands:5, Ten thousands:6, Hundred thousands:3, Millions:1, Ten millions:0, Hundred millions:5, and the final carryover 1. So the total is 1 followed by 5, then 0,1,3,6,5,9,3,0.\n\nWait, let me write that properly:.\n\nStarting from the highest place:.\n\nThe carryover 1 is the billions place, then 5 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (units).\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I need to arrange them in order. Let me reconstruct the sum step by step.\n\nAfter adding each digit, the digits from right to left (units to hundred millions plus the carryover) are:.\n\nUnits: 0.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nHundred thousands:3.\n\nMillions:1.\n\nTen millions:0.\n\nHundred millions:5.\n\nBillions place:1 (from the carryover).\n\nSo writing the number from billions down to units:.\n\n1 (billions), 5 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
