nDigit 7:7.\n\nDigit 8:7.\n\nDigit 9:6.\n\nSecond number:586,737,561.\n\nBreaking into digits:.\n\nDigit 1 (rightmost):1.\n\nDigit 2:6.\n\nDigit 3:5.\n\nDigit 4:7.\n\nDigit 5:3.\n\nDigit 6:7.\n\nDigit 7:6.\n\nDigit 8:8.\n\nDigit 9:5.\n\nWait, let me confirm:.\n\nThe second number is 586,737,561.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nDigit 1:1 (units).\n\nDigit 2:6 (tens).\n\nDigit 3:5 (hundreds).\n\nDigit 4:7 (thousands).\n\nDigit 5:3 (ten thousands).\n\nDigit 6:7 (hundred thousands).\n\nDigit 7:6 (millions).\n\nDigit 8:8 (ten millions).\n\nDigit 9:5 (hundred millions).\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nNow, adding digit by digit starting from the right (units):.\n\nDigit 1: 6 + 1 =7. Write down 7.\n\nDigit 2:2 +6=8. Write 8.\n\nDigit3:4 +5=9. Write 9.\n\nDigit4:7 +7=14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nDigit5:3 +3 +1(carry)=7. Write 7.\n\nDigit6:7 +7=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nDigit7:7 (from first number) +6 (second number)=13. Plus carryover1 makes 14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nDigit8:7 (first number) +8 (second number)=15. Plus carryover1=16. Write6, carryover1.\n\nDigit9:6 (first number) +5 (second number)=11. Plus carryover1=12. Write2, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the final carryover1 becomes the next digit (the 10th digit). So the total digits are 10 digits.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the highest digit:.\n\nThe carried over 1, then the digit9 result is 2, digit8 is6, digit7 is4, digit6 is4, digit5 is7, digit4 is4, digit3 is9, digit2 is8, digit1 is7.\n\nSo the number is:.\n\n1 (billions place), 2 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands),7 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),9 (hundreds),8 (tens),7 (units).\n\nWait, let me structure it properly:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:2.\n\nTen millions:6.\n\nMillions:4.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:8.\n\nUnits:7.\n\nSo the number is 1,264,749,87? Wait, maybe I need to write it with commas correctly.\n\