lace and carryover 1 to a new billion place. But since both numbers are 9 digits, the result will be a 10-digit number. So the total would be:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits we have are:.\n\nPosition1:0  .\nPosition2:5  .\nPosition3:6  .\nPosition4:1  .\nPosition5:5  .\nPosition6:5  .\nPosition7:0  .\nPosition8:4  .\nPosition9:0  .\nPlus the carryover 1 to the next (10th) digit.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be:.\n\n1 (from the carryover) followed by the digits from position9 to position1:.\n\nWait, let me retrace:.\n\nAfter adding each position, starting from the right:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1 (units): 0  .\n2 (tens):5  .\n3 (hundreds):6  .\n4 (thousands):1  .\n5 (ten thousands):5  .\n6 (hundred thousands):5  .\n7 (millions):0  .\n8 (ten millions):4  .\n9 (hundred millions):0 (since 1+9 + the carryover? Wait, actually, let's track step by step again to avoid confusion.\n\nLet me redo the addition step by step carefully.\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically aligned:.\n\n       1 1 3 2 0 8 7 2 3  .\n     + 9 2 7 3 4 2 9 2 7  .\n     ----------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):.\n\n3 +7 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nNext digit (tens place):.\n\n2 +2 =4, plus the carryover 1 =5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nNext (hundreds place):.\n\n7 +9 =16. Write 6, carryover1.\n\nNext (thousands place):.\n\n8 +2 =10, plus carryover1 =11. Write 1, carryover1.\n\nNext (ten thousands place):.\n\n0 +4 =4, plus carryover1 =5. Write 5.\n\nNext (hundred thousands place):.\n\n2 +3 =5. Write5.\n\nNext (millions place):.\n\n3 +7 =10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nNext (ten millions place):.\n\n1 +2 =3, plus carryover1 =4. Write4.\n\nNext (hundred millions place):.\n\n1 +9 =10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, we add the final carryover1 at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from left to right are:.\n\n1 (carryover), followed by 0 (from hundred millions), then 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions),5 (hundr