6:7,.\n\nPosition5:4,.\n\nPosition4:0,.\n\nPosition3:2,.\n\nPosition2:1,.\n\nPosition1:4,.\n\nPosition0:0.\n\nWait, so arranging from the highest position to the lowest:.\n\nPosition9:1,.\n\nPosition8:9,.\n\nPosition7:2,.\n\nPosition6:7,.\n\nPosition5:4,.\n\nPosition4:0,.\n\nPosition3:2,.\n\nPosition2:1,.\n\nPosition1:4,.\n\nPosition0:0.\n\nSo writing them all together:.\n\n1 9 2 7 4 0 2 1 4 0.\n\nWait, that would be 1,927,402,140?.\n\nWait, let me count the digits:.\n\nStarting from the left:.\n\n1 (billion?), then 9 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 0 (units). .\n\nWait, so the number is 1,927,402,140?.\n\nWait, but let me check again step by step.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the positions. Let me try a different approach. Let me add the numbers digit by digit with commas.\n\nFirst number: 988,964,979.\n\nSecond number: 937,537,161.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nLet's split into parts:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 9 +1 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 7 +6 =13 +1=14. 4, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:9+1=10 +1=11. 1, carryover1.\n\nThousands:4 +7=11 +1=12. 2, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:6 +3=9 +1=10. 0, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:8 +5=13 +1=14. 4, carryover1.\n\nMillions:9 +7=16 +1=17. 7, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:8 +3=11 +1=12. 2, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:9 +9=18 +1=19. 9, carryover1.\n\nThen the final carryover 1 becomes the billions place.\n\nSo the total is 1,927,402,140?.\n\nWait, let me see:.\n\nBreaking down the result digit by digit:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nTens:4.\n\nUnits:0.\n\nYes, so the number is 1,927,402,140.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method. Maybe adding them as whole numbers step by step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the two numbers in parts.\n\nFirst number: 988,964,979.\n\nSecond number: 937,537,161.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nLet me see:.\n\nStart with 988,964,979 + 900,000,000 = 1,888,964,979.\n\nBut that's not helpful. Alternatively, adding the millions:.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers digit by digit again to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, let me use a calculator approach mentally.\n\nWait, 988,964,979 + 937,537,161.\n\nLet me add the millions first:.\n\n988,964,979 is 988 million plus 964,979.\n\n937,537,161 is 937 million plus 537,161.\n\nAdding the millions: 988 + 937 = ?.\n\n988 + 900 = 1888, then +37 = 1925. So 1,925,000,000.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 964,979 + 537,161.\n\nAdding those:.\n\n964,979 + 500,000 = 1,464,979.\n\nThen adding 37,161: 1,464,979 + 37,161 = 1,502,140. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
