t digit (ones place):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):5.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):0.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):6.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):5.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):4.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):7.\n\nPosition7 (millions):6.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3 (since 6+7=13, we wrote 3 here and carried over 1).\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):3+3+1=7.\n\nSo the total number would be 7 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),6 (hundreds),0 (tens),5 (ones). Wait, but hold on, let me check the order again.\n\nWait the places are:.\n\nPosition 9: hundred millions (the leftmost digit).\n\nPosition8: ten millions.\n\nPosition7: millions.\n\nPosition6: hundred thousands.\n\nPosition5: ten thousands.\n\nPosition4: thousands.\n\nPosition3: hundreds.\n\nPosition2: tens.\n\nPosition1: ones.\n\nSo the digits from left to right are:.\n\nPosition9:7,.\n\nPosition8:3,.\n\nPosition7:6,.\n\nPosition6:7,.\n\nPosition5:4,.\n\nPosition4:5,.\n\nPosition3:6,.\n\nPosition2:0,.\n\nPosition1:5. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
