7. Write 7, carryover 1.\nHundreds place: 9 + 7 = 16, plus 1 carried over is 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\nThousands place: 4 (from first number) + 8 (from second) = 12, plus 1 is 13. Write 3, carryover 1.\nTen-thousands place: 4 + 1 = 5, plus 1 carried over is 6. Write 6, no carryover.\nHundred-thousands place: 5 (from first number) + 6 (from second) = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\nMillions place: 3 (from first number) + 5 (from second) = 8, plus 1 carried over is 9. Write 9, no carryover.\nTen-millions place: 1 (from first number) + 9 (from second) = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\nHundred-millions place: 3 (from first number) + 5 (from second) = 8, plus 1 carried over is 9. Write 9.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left, with the carried-over digits, the result should be:.\n\n9 (hundred-millions) 0 (ten-millions) 9 (millions) 1 (hundred-thousands) 6 (ten-thousands) 3 (thousands) 7 (hundreds) 7 (tens) 9 (units). Wait, maybe I need to check again step by step.\n\nWait, let me redo the addition step by step carefully:.\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically:.\n\n          3 1 3 5 4 4 9 8 6.\n        + 5 9 5 6 1 8 7 9 3.\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):.\n\n6 (units) + 3 (units) = 9. Write 9.\n\nNext digit (tens place): 8 + 9 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nNext (hundreds place): 9 + 7 = 16 + 1 (carry) = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 4 + 8 = 12 + 1 =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 +1 =5 +1 =6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 5 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: 3 (from first number) +5 (from second number) =8 +1 (carryover) =9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen-millions place:1 (from first number) +9 (from second number)=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-millions place: 3 (from first number) +5 (from second number)=8 +1 (carryover)=9. Write 9.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nUnits:9, tens:7, hundreds:7, thousands:3, ten-thousands:6, hundred-thousands:1, millions:9, ten-millions:0, hundred-millions:9. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 44%|####4     | 221/500 [6:33:15<6:38:13, 85.64s/it] 44%|####4     | 222/500 [6:33:59<5:39:49, 73.34s/it]
