carryover.\n\n4. Thousands place: 0 + 6 =6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\n5. Ten thousands place: 6 (from first) + 3 (from second) =9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place: 3 (first) +4 (second)=7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\n7. Millions place: 2 (first) + 2 (second)=4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\n8. Ten millions place: 2 (first) +3 (second)=5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:5 (first) +7 (second)=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nWait, but the hundred millions place is the leftmost digit. Since adding 5 and 7 gives 12, we need to write 2 in the hundred millions place and carry over 1 to a new billion place. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
