1 = 6. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 5 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 + 6 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 8 + 1 = 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: 4 + 4 = 8 + 1 = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen-millions place: 9 + 8 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-millions place: 5 + 2 = 7 + 1 = 8. Write 8.\n\nSo the result is 8 7 9 0 0 1 6 7 1, which is 879,001,671.\n\nBut the second method gave 879,001,573. That's a difference in the thousands and hundreds place? Wait, let me see:\n\nWait in the second method, when adding 594,836,598 and 284,165,073:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nFirst number: 594,836,598 is 500,000,000 + 94,000,000 + 800,000 + 36,000 + 500 + 98\n\nSecond number: 284,165,073 is 200,000,000 + 84,000,000 + 100,000 + 65,000 + 73\n\nAdding each part:\n\n500M + 200M = 700M\n\n94M +84M = 178M \u2192 total so far 878M\n\n800k +100k = 900k \u2192 878,900,000\n\n36k +65k = 101k \u2192 878,900,000 + 101,000 = 879,001,000\n\n500 +73 = 573 \u2192 total 879,001,573\n\nHmm, so according to this breakdown, the total is 879,001,573. But in the column addition, it's 879,001,671.\n\nWait, where's the mistake here? Let me check the breakdown again.\n\nWait, the first number is 594,836,598.\n\nBreaking down into components:\n\n500,000,000\n\n94,000,000 (since 594,000,000 minus 500,000,000 is 94,000,000)\n\nThen 836,598 left. Breaking that down: 800,000 + 36,000 + 598.\n\nWait, but in the breakdown above, it's written as 800,000 + 36,000 + 500 + 98. That's correct, because 598 is 500 +98.\n\nBut the second number is 284,165,073.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n200,000,000\n\n84,000,000 (since 284,000,000 minus 200,000,000 is 84,000,000)\n\nThen 165,073 left: 100,000 + 65,000 + 73. That's correct.\n\nSo adding:\n\n500M +200M=700M\n\n94M+84M=178M \u2192 878M\n\n800k +100k=900k \u2192878,900k?\n\nWait, 878,900,000 + 900,000 would be 879,800,000? Wait no, wait 878,000,000 + 900,000 is 878,900,000?\n\n