3+5=8 +1=9. Write9, carryover0.\n\nTen thousands (position5):.\n\nFirst:8, second:7. 8+7=15. Write5, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands (position6):.\n\nFirst:2, second:5. 2+5=7 +1=8. Write8, carryover0.\n\nMillions (position7):.\n\nFirst:5, second:4. 5+4=9. Write9, carryover0.\n\nTen millions (position8):.\n\nFirst:9, second:1. 9+1=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions (position9):.\n\nFirst:6, second:3. 6+3=9 +1(carryover)=10. So here, since this is the leftmost digit, we have to add the 10. So we write 0 and carryover1, but since there are no more digits, the carryover becomes a new digit at the front.\n\nTherefore, the total is 1 followed by the digits we have so far.\n\nPutting it all together from last to first:.\n\nStarting from the units, the digits we wrote were:.\n\nPosition1:7, pos2:8, pos3:6, pos4:9, pos5:5, pos6:8, pos7:9, pos8:0, pos9:0, and then the final carryover1.\n\nWait, actually, the positions are from right to left, so when we write the result, the digits should be arranged from the last carryover to the first digits.\n\nWait, let me structure this properly:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units) which is position1, the result digits are:.\n\nPosition1:7.\n\nPosition2:8.\n\nPosition3:6.\n\nPosition4:9.\n\nPosition5:5.\n\nPosition6:8.\n\nPosition7:9.\n\nPosition8:0.\n\nPosition9:0 (from the hundred millions place before carryover).\n\nBut we had a carryover of 1 from the hundred millions addition (position9), so that adds an extra digit to the left of the hundred millions place, making it 1 followed by the 0 from position9, so the digits would be:.\n\n1 (from carryover), then the digit from position9 (0), then position8 (0), etc. Wait, perhaps I need to list all digits in order.\n\nWait, maybe I need to consider that each position corresponds to a digit place. Let's see:.\n\nThe final sum is:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n7 (units),.\n\n8 (tens),.\n\n6 (hundreds),.\n\n9 (thousands),.\n\n5 (ten thousands),.\n\n8 (hundred thousands),.\n\n9 (millions),.\n\n0 (ten millions),.\n\n0 (hundred millions),.\n\nplus the carryover 1 which is the billions place. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
