te 8.\n\nFifth digit (ten thousands place):.\n1 + 7 = 8. Write 8.\n\nSixth digit (hundred thousands place):.\n6 + 3 = 9. Write 9.\n\nSeventh digit (millions place):.\n2 + 5 = 7. Write 7.\n\nEighth digit (ten millions place):.\n2 + 2 = 4. Write 4.\n\nNinth digit (hundred millions place):.\n2 + 1 = 3. Write 3.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left, we have:.\n\n3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 1 (ones). Wait, let me check that again. Wait, no, when writing the result, the digits are from the highest place to the lowest, so the digits we wrote are:.\n\nStarting from the left (hundred millions place): 3, then ten millions:4, millions:7, hundred thousands:9, ten thousands:8, thousands:8, hundreds:7, tens:1, ones:1. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
