ion 8 (ten millions):9 +0=9.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):4 +6=10, so write 0 and carryover 1.\n\nThen the carryover 1 becomes the next digit (billions place:1).\n\nSo putting all digits together from left to right:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:0.\n\nTen millions:9.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:8.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nTens:3.\n\nUnits:8. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 56%|#####6    | 281/500 [8:09:04<5:04:16, 83.36s/it]
