 the right, the digits we have are:.\n\nBillions: 1.\n\nHundred millions: 2.\n\nTen millions: 3.\n\nMillions: 2.\n\nHundred thousands: 7.\n\nTen thousands: 9.\n\nThousands: 9.\n\nHundreds: 2.\n\nTens: 4.\n\nOnes: 3.\n\nSo combining these:.\n\n1 (billion), 2 (hundred million), 3 (ten million), 2 (million), then 7 (hundred thousand), 9 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 4 (ten), 3 (one). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
