eds), 0 (thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 1 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 2 (ten millions), 4 (hundred millions).\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\n          4 4 3 3 6 5 4 6 3.\n\n        + 4 2 8 1 6 0 0 6 7.\n\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 3 +7 =10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nTens:6 +6=12 +1=13. Write 3, carry1.\n\nHundreds:4 +0=4 +1=5. Write5, no carry.\n\nThousands:5 +0=5. Write5.\n\nTen thousands:6 +6=12. Write2, carry1.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +1=4 +1=5. Write5.\n\nMillions:3 +8=11. Wait, here's a problem. Let me check again:.\n\nWait, in millions place, first number has 3 (million digit), and second has 8 (million digit). So 3 +8=11. So write 1 and carry over 1.\n\nTen millions place:4 (from first number) +2 (from second) +1 (carry)=7. Write7.\n\nHundred millions place:4 +4=8. Write8.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits we got are:.\n\nUnits:0.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:5.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nHundred thousands:5.\n\nMillions:1 (with a carryover).\n\nWait, let me list all the digits step by step:.\n\nLet me go step by step again carefully.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n1. Units place: 3 +7 =10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\n2. Tens place:6 +6 =12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:4 +0 =4 +1=5 →5, no carry.\n\n4. Thousands place:5 +0=5 →5.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:6 +6=12 →2, carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:3 +1=4 +1=5 →5, no carry.\n\n7. Millions place:3 (from first number) +8 (from second number)=11 →1, carryover1.\n\n8. Ten millions place:4 (first) +2 (second) +1 (carry) =7 →7.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:4 +4=8 →8.\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left:.\n\nStarting from units:0, then 3,5,5,2,5,1,7,8.\n\nWait, actually, the digits should be in the order of units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, hundred millions.\n\nSo the result digits from right to left are:.\n\n0 (units),.\n\n3 (tens)