ace).\nDigit 2: 5 (ten millions).\nDigit 3: 7 (millions).\nDigit 4: 6 (hundred thousands).\nDigit 5: 0 (ten thousands).\nDigit 6: 7 (thousands).\nDigit 7: 7 (hundreds).\nDigit 8: 3 (tens).\nDigit 9: 2 (ones).\n\nWait, actually, standard place values:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nDigit 1: ones place (2).\nDigit 2: tens (3).\nDigit 3: hundreds (7).\nDigit 4: thousands (7).\nDigit 5: ten thousands (0).\nDigit 6: hundred thousands (6).\nDigit 7: millions (7).\nDigit 8: ten millions (5).\nDigit 9: hundred millions (7).\n\nSimilarly, the second number 195,828,483:.\n\nDigit 1: 3 (ones).\nDigit 2: 8 (tens).\nDigit 3: 4 (hundreds).\nDigit 4: 8 (thousands).\nDigit 5: 2 (ten thousands).\nDigit 6: 8 (hundred thousands).\nDigit 7: 5 (millions).\nDigit 8: 9 (ten millions).\nDigit 9: 1 (hundred millions).\n\nSo when adding, let me align them properly:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\nFirst number: 2.\nSecond number: 3.\nSum: 2 + 3 = 5. Write 5.\n\nTens place:.\n\nFirst number: 3.\nSecond number: 8.\nSum: 3 + 8 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\n\nFirst number: 7.\nSecond number: 4.\nPlus carryover 1: 7 + 4 +1 =12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:.\n\nFirst number: 7.\nSecond number:8.\nPlus 1: 7 +8 +1=16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n\nFirst number:0.\nSecond number:2.\nPlus 1: 0+2+1=3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n\nFirst number:6.\nSecond number:8.\n6+8=14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place:.\n\nFirst number:7.\nSecond number:5.\nPlus 1:7+5+1=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen millions place:.\n\nFirst number:5.\nSecond number:9.\nPlus 1:5+9+1=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions place:.\n\nFirst number:7.\nSecond number:1.\nPlus 1:7+1+1=9. Write 9.\n\nSo putting all together, the sum is:.\n\nFrom right to left, the digits we wrote are:.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTens:1.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nWait, but we need to arrange them from left to right as numbers. So starting from the highest place:.\n\nHundred millions place:9, ten millions:5, millions:3, hundred thousands:4, ten thousands:3, thousands:6, hundreds:2, tens:1, ones:5. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
