ave a carryover of 1 from the hundred millions place, we need to add a new digit to the left (billions place) which is 1.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits are:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions:7.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nHundred thousands:0.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nTens:1.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nWait, but when we write it out, the order should be:.\n\nStarting from the highest place, which is billions, then hundred millions, ten millions, millions, etc. So the number would be:.\n\n1 (billions), 7 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
