thousands): 8 + 1 = 9 + 1 (carryover) = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 6 (Hundred thousands): 6 + 1 = 7 + 1 (carryover) = 8. Write 8.\n\nPosition 7 (Millions): 1 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 8. Write 8.\n\nPosition 8 (Ten millions): 2 + 6 = 8. Write 8.\n\nPosition 9 (Hundred millions): 7 + 9 = 16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover 1 after the hundred millions place, we need to add another digit at the beginning. So the total sum is 1 followed by the digits we've written.\n\nPutting all the digits together from last to first:.\n\nThe carryover 1 is the next digit, so the digits are:.\n\n1 (from carryover), then 6 (hundred millions place), then 8 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 7 (ones). Wait, no, let me check the order.\n\nWait, when we write the digits from right to left, the positions are:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 7  .\nPosition 2 (tens): 8  .\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 0  .\nPosition 4 (thousands): 0  .\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 0  .\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 8  .\nPosition 7 (millions): 8  .\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8  .\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 6  .\nPlus the carryover 1 as the billions place.\n\nSo arranging them from highest to lowest place:.\n\nBillions place: 1  .\nHundred millions: 6  .\nTen millions: 8  .\nMillions: 8  .\nHundred thousands: 8  .\nTen thousands: 0  .\nThousands: 0  .\nHundreds: 0  .\nTens: 8  .\nOnes: 7  .\n\nWait, let me see. Wait, the positions after adding:.\n\nAfter the hundred millions digit (position 9) we had 16, so that gives 6 in the hundred millions and carryover 1 to the billions place. So the billions digit is 1. Then the rest:.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8  .\nPosition 7 (millions):8  .\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):8  .\nPosition5 (ten thousands):0  .\nPosition4 (thousands):0  .\nPosition3 (hundreds):0  .\nPosition2 (tens):8  .\nPosition1 (ones):7  .\n\nWait, but when written in orde