s place), 0 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 196,008,416. Breaking down:.\n\n1 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\nHundred millions: 4 vs 1.\n\nTen millions: 0 vs 9.\n\nMillions: 1 vs 6.\n\nHundred thousands: 4 vs 0.\n\nTen thousands: 9 vs 0.\n\nThousands: 2 vs 8.\n\nHundreds: 4 vs 4.\n\nTens: 5 vs 1.\n\nOnes: 0 vs 6.\n\nWait, maybe writing vertically:.\n\n          4 0 1 4 9 2 4 5 0.\n\n        + 1 9 6 0 0 8 4 1 6.\n\n        -------------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\n0 + 6 = 6.\n\n5 + 1 = 6.\n\n4 + 4 = 8.\n\n2 + 8 = 10 (write 0, carryover 1).\n\n9 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 10 (write 0, carryover 1).\n\n4 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 5 (wait, 4 (from first number) + 0 (from second) + 1 carried over = 5? Wait, but the hundred thousands place: first number has 4, second has 0, so 4+0=4 plus carryover 1 is 5. Then next is millions place:.\n\n1 (from first number) + 6 (from second) = 7, no carryover.\n\nThen ten millions place: 0 (from first) + 9 (from second) = 9.\n\nHundred millions place: 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nWait, so putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits would be:.\n\n0 (ones), 6 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 0 (thousands with a carryover), then 0 (ten thousands with a carryover), 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 5 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, let me reconstruct step by step.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n1st digit (ones): 0 +6 =6.\n\n2nd digit (tens):5+1=6.\n\n3rd digit (hundreds):4+4=8.\n\n4th digit (thousands):2+8=10, so write 0, carryover 1.\n\n5th digit (ten thousands):9 + 0 +1 (carryover)=10, so write 0, carryover 1.\n\n6th digit (hundred thousands):4 +0 +1 (carryover)=5.\n\n7th digit (millions):1 +6=7.\n\n8th digit (ten millions):0 +9=9.\n\n9th digit (hundred millions):4 +1=5.\n\nSo the total digits from right to left would be:.\n\n6 (ones), 6 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 5 (hundred millions).\n\nTherefore, writing the number from left to right (hundred millions to ones):.\n\n5 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nWait, hold on, let me check that again. The digits from right to left as we calculated were:.\n\n6 (ones), 6 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 5 (hundred millions).\n\nSo reversing that order for the actual number, it's 5 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones). So putting commas in the right places:. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
