right to left, carrying over as needed:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  341,993,509 \\\\\n+ 119,181,885 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\n1. **Ones place**: \\(9 + 5 = 14\\) \u2192 Write 4, carry over 1.\n2. **Tens place**: \\(0 + 8 + 1 = 9\\) \u2192 Write 9.\n3. **Hundreds place**: \\(5 + 8 = 13\\) \u2192 Write 3, carry over 1.\n4. **Thousands place**: \\(3 + 1 + 1 = 5\\) \u2192 Write 5.\n5. **Ten thousands place**: \\(9 + 8 = 17\\) \u2192 Write 7, carry over 1.\n6. **Hundred thousands place**: \\(9 + 1 + 1 = 11\\) \u2192 Write 1, carry over 1.\n7. **Millions place**: \\(1 + 9 + 1 = 11\\) \u2192 Write 1, carry over 1.\n8. **Ten millions place**: \\(4 + 1 + 1 = 6\\) \u2192 Write 6.\n9. **Hundred millions place**: \\(3 + 1 = 4\\) \u2192 Write 4.\n\nCombining all the digits from left to right, we get the result: 461,175,394.\n\nTo verify, we can break the numbers into parts:\n- \\(341,993,509 = 341,000,000 + 993,509\\)\n- \\(119,181,885 = 119,000,000 + 181,885\\)\n\nAdding the parts separately:\n- \\(341,000,000 + 119,000,000 = 460,000,000\\)\n- \\(993,509 + 181,885 = 1,175,394\\)\n\nSumming these results:\n- \\(460,000,000 + 1,175,394 = 461,175,394\\)\n\nThus, the sum of 341,993,509 and 119,181,885 is \\(\\boxed{461175394}\\).",
