tal digits are:.\n\nPosition10:1.\n\nPosition9:4.\n\nPosition8:1.\n\nPosition7:2.\n\nPosition6:0.\n\nPosition5:0.\n\nPosition4:8.\n\nPosition3:4.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition1:0.\n\nWait, this is getting confusing. Let me list the digits in order from left to right (billions place first):.\n\nThe first digit (billions place) is the carried over 1 from the hundred millions addition. Then the next digits are from the previous additions:.\n\nSo starting from the highest digit:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions place:4 (from 14).\n\nTen millions place:1 (from digit8's result).\n\nMillions place:2 (from digit7).\n\nHundred thousands place:0 (digit6).\n\nTen thousands place:0 (digit5).\n\nThousands place:8 (digit4).\n\nHundreds place:4 (digit3).\n\nTens place:3 (digit2).\n\nUnits place:0 (digit1).\n\nSo putting that all together:.\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 0 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
