ns), 0 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (hundred thousands), 2 (millions),6 (ten millions),4 (hundred millions), and 1 (billions). So the number is 1,462,908,070. That seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like splitting the numbers into smaller parts.\n\n936,291,627 is 900,000,000 + 36,000,000 + 291,627.\n\n526,616,443 is 500,000,000 + 26,000,000 + 616,443.\n\nAdding the hundreds millions:\n\n900M +500M =1,400M.\n\n36M +26M =62M. So total so far:1,462M.\n\nNow the remaining parts: 291,627 +616,443.\n\n291,627 +616,443:\n\nLet's add 291k +616k =907k, and 627 +443=1,070.\n\nWait, 291,627 + 616,443:\n\nFirst, 291,627 + 616,443:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n200,000 + 600,000 =800,000.\n\n91,000 +16,000 =107,000.\n\n600 +400 =1,000.\n\n27 +43 =70.\n\nAdding all those:800k +107k =907k, plus 1,000 is 908k, plus 70 is 908,070. So total is 1,462,000,000 +908,070 =1,462,908,070. Same result again.\n\nHmm, so it seems like the answer is 1,462,908,070. But let me just do a quick check using approximate rounding to see if it makes sense.\n\n936 million plus 526 million is roughly 1,462 million, which is 1.462 billion. Then adding the remaining parts, which are 291,627 and 616,443. Adding those gives about 908,000. So total is 1.462 billion plus 0.908 million, so total is approximately 1.462908 billion, which matches the exact result. So that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use calculator-like step-by-step addition:\n\nLet me write both numbers without commas:\n\n936291627\n\n+526616443\n\n------------.\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nDigit positions (from right, starting at 1):\n\n1: 7 +3 =10\n\n2:2+4=6 +1=7\n\n3:6+4=10\n\n4:1+6=7 +1=8\n\n5:9+1=10\n\n6:2+6=8 +1=9\n\n7:6+6=12\n\n8:3+2=5 +1=6\n\n9:9+5=14\n\nSo writing the digits from right to left with carries:\n\nPositions:\n\n1:0, carry 1\n\n2:7, carry 0\n\n3:0, carry1\n\n4:8, carry0\n\n5:0, carry1\n\n6:9, carry0\n\n7:2, carry1\n\n8:6, carry0\n\n9:4, carry1\n\nTh