ryover becomes a new digit at the front.\n\nWait, so the total would be 1 6 followed by the rest? Wait let me retrace.\n\nWait, digit 9 (hundred millions place):.\n\n9 +7 =16. So we write 6 in the hundred millions place, and carryover 1 to the next (billions) place. Since there's no higher digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning. So the total digits would be 10 digits now.\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the highest digit:.\n\nCarryover 1 (billions place), then 6 (hundred millions), then the results from digits 8 down:.\n\nDigit 8 (ten millions): 0.\n\nDigit 7 (millions):5.\n\nDigit 6 (hundred thousands):4.\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):7.\n\nDigit4 (thousands):5.\n\nDigit3 (hundreds):3.\n\nDigit2 (tens):6.\n\nDigit1 (units):3.\n\nSo the total number is:.\n\n1 (billions) 6 (hundred millions) 0 (ten millions) 5 (millions) 4 (hundred thousands) 7 (ten thousands) 5 (thousands) 3 (hundreds) 6 (tens) 3 (units). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
