0.\n      + 5 0 2 3 3 4 3 0 7.\n      --------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):.\n\n0 +7 =7.\n\nTens place:2 +0 =2.\n\nHundreds place:8 +3 =11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:2 +4 =6, plus carryover 1 =7.\n\nTen thousands place:5 +3 =8.\n\nHundred thousands place:6 +3 =9.\n\nMillions place:2 +2 =4.\n\nTen millions place:9 +0 =9? Wait, hold on. Wait the second number's ten millions place is the second digit from the left. Let me check again.\n\nWait, let me list each digit position properly.\n\nLet me number the digits from right to left as positions 1 to 9.\n\nFirst number: 892,652,820.\n\nDigits from right (position 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition 1 (units):0.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):2.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):8.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):2.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):5.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):6.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):2.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):9.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):8.\n\nSecond number:502,334,307.\n\nDigits from right:.\n\nPosition 1:7.\n\nPosition 2:0.\n\nPosition 3:3.\n\nPosition 4:4.\n\nPosition 5:3.\n\nPosition 6:3.\n\nPosition 7:2.\n\nPosition 8:0.\n\nPosition 9:5.\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nPosition 1:0+7=7.\n\nPosition 2:2+0=2.\n\nPosition 3:8+3=11 (write 1, carryover 1).\n\nPosition 4:2+4=6 +1=7.\n\nPosition 5:5+3=8.\n\nPosition 6:6+3=9.\n\nPosition 7:2+2=4.\n\nPosition 8:9+0=9.\n\nPosition 9:8+5=13 (write 3, carryover 1, but since there are no more digits, add the carryover as a new digit).\n\nWait, hold on. When adding position 9 (hundred millions place), we have 8 +5 =13. But since both numbers only have 9 digits, the carryover from the hundred millions would create a 10th digit (billions place). So the result would have 10 digits.\n\nSo the total sum would be:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPosition 1:7.\n\nPosition 2:2.\n\nPosition 3:1 (with carryover 1 to next).\n\nPosition 4:7.\n\nPosition 5:8.\n\nPosition 6:9.\n\nPosition 7:4.\n\nPosition 8:9.\n\nPosition 9:3 (from 13) with a