---------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):.\n\n6 + 0 = 6 (units place).\n\nThen moving left:.\n\n3 (tens) + 3 (tens) = 6 (tens place).\n\n1 (hundreds) + 6 (hundreds) = 7 (hundreds place).\n\n0 (thousands) + 7 (thousands) = 7 (thousands place).\n\n3 (ten thousands) + 4 (ten thousands) = 7 (ten thousands place).\n\n1 (hundred thousands) + 5 (hundred thousands) = 6 (hundred thousands place).\n\n2 (millions) + 1 (millions) = 3 (millions place).\n\n8 (ten millions) + 0 (ten millions) = 8 (ten millions place).\n\n2 (hundred millions) + 6 (hundred millions) = 8 (hundred millions place).\n\nWait, but hold on, let me check each column again step by step to ensure there are no mistakes.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits column: 6 + 0 = 6. Write down 6.\n\nTens column: 3 + 3 = 6. Write down 6.\n\nHundreds column: 1 + 6 = 7. Write down 7.\n\nThousands column: 0 + 7 = 7. Write down 7.\n\nTen-thousands column: 3 (from first number) + 4 (from second number) = 7. So 7.\n\nHundred-thousands column: 1 (from first) + 5 (from second) = 6. .\n\nMillions column: 2 (from first) + 1 (from second) = 3.\n\nTen-millions column: 8 (first) + 0 (second) = 8.\n\nHundred-millions column: 2 (first) + 6 (second) = 8. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
