lions), 2 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 3 (ones).\n\nYes, so when adding the hundred millions place: 9 + 9 = 18. So that would give an 8 in the hundred millions place and carry over 1 to the next higher place, which is the billions place. Since there are no more digits, that carried-over 1 becomes a 1 in the billions place. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
