eck the order:.\n\nWait, the positions are:.\n\nPosition1: units (5).\n\nPosition2: tens (7).\n\nPosition3: hundreds (1).\n\nPosition4: thousands (3).\n\nPosition5: ten thousands (2).\n\nPosition6: hundred thousands (3).\n\nPosition7: millions (2).\n\nPosition8: ten millions (7).\n\nPosition9: hundred millions (1).\n\nPlus the carryover to billions (1).\n\nSo the number is:.\n\n1 (billions), 1 (hundred millions),7 (ten millions),2 (millions),3 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),1 (hundreds),7 (tens),5 (units). .\n\nSo writing that out:.\n\n1,172,323,175?.\n\nWait, let's see:.\n\nBreaking into groups:.\n\nBillions: 1.\n\nHundred millions: 1.\n\nTen millions:7.\n\nMillions:2.\n\nHundred thousands:3.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nTens:7.\n\nUnits:5.\n\nSo combining:.\n\n1,172,323,175. Let me check that.\n\nWait, 1 billion, 172 million, 323 thousand, 175. Wait, maybe better to write in standard commas:.\n\n1,172,323,175.\n\nBut let me confirm with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers using another approach.\n\nFirst number: 831,100,114.\n\nSecond number: 359,223,061.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nLet me try adding the numbers in parts.\n\nBreakdown:.\n\n831,100,114 + 359,223,061.\n\nLet me separate the numbers into millions and the rest:.\n\nFirst number: 831 million + 100,114.\n\nSecond number: 359 million + 223,061.\n\nAdding the millions: 831 + 359 = 1,190 millions.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 100,114 + 223,061 = ?.\n\n100,114 + 223,061:.\n\nAdding units: 4 +1=5.\n\nTens:1+6=7.\n\nHundreds:1+0=1.\n\nThousands:0+3=3.\n\nTen thousands:0+2=2.\n\nHundred thousands:1+2=3 (Wait, let's do it properly:.\n\n100,114 is:.\n\n100,114 = 1 hundred thousand (100,000) + 114.\n\n223,061 is 2 hundred thousand (200,000) + 23,061.\n\nSo adding:.\n\n100,000 + 200,000 = 300,000.\n\n114 +23,061 = 23,175.\n\nTotal: 300,000 +23,175 = 323,175.\n\nTherefore total of both parts:. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
