. Hmm, here we get 11. So write 1, carry over 1.\n\nDigit 8 (ten millions place):5 +7 =12, plus the carried over 1 =13. So write 3, carry over 1.\n\nDigit 9 (hundred millions place):8 +7 =15, plus the carried over 1 =16. So write 6, carry over 1. But wait, there are no more digits, so we have to add that 1 as a new digit on the left.\n\nWait, let me check again step by step. Let me write down each digit's addition with carries:.\n\nLet me tabulate this properly.\n\nLet me list each position from right to left with their digits and the sum:.\n\nPosition 1 (units): 7 +7 =14 → 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):6 +7 =13 +1 =14 →4, carryover1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):7+9=16 +1=17→7, carryover1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):0+4=4 +1=5→5, no carryover.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):5 +1=6→6.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2+0=2→2.\n\nPosition7 (millions):5+6=11→1, carryover1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5+7=12 +1=13→3, carryover1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8+7=15 +1=16→6, carryover1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, we have to add the final carryover of 1 as the next digit. So the total sum would be:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit we calculated:.\n\nPositions 1-9 give us the digits from right to left as follows:.\n\nPosition1:4.\n\nPosition2:4.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:5.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition6:2.\n\nPosition7:1.\n\nPosition8:3.\n\nPosition9:6.\n\nPlus the final carryover 1 at the next position (the billions place).\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits from right to left are:.\n\n4 (units), 4 (tens), 7 (hundreds),5 (thousands),6 (ten thousands),2 (hundred thousands),1 (millions),3 (ten millions),6 (hundred millions), and then the 1 in the billions place.\n\nTherefore, writing the number from left to right, starting with the billions digit:.\n\n1 (billions), 6 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions),1 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),7 (hundreds),4 (tens),4 (units). .\n\nWait, let me make sure I'm arranging th