01,558\n\n-    963,134,105\n\nTo subtract, we can align them:\n\n1,784,901,558\n\n-\u00a0  963,134,105\n\n-----------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nUnits:8-5=3\n\nTens:5-0=5\n\nHundreds:5-1=4\n\nThousands:1-4. Can't do, need to borrow.\n\nThe thousands digit is 1, and we need to subtract 4. So borrow from the ten thousands place.\n\nTen thousands place in the minuend (first number) is 0, so need to go to the next non-zero digit. The hundred thousands place is 9. So borrow 1 from the 9 (making it 8), then the ten thousands place becomes 10 (since we moved a borrow through the ten thousands). Then, borrow 1 from ten thousands (now 10 becomes 9) to the thousands place, making it 11.\n\nNow, thousands place:11-4=7\n\nTen thousands place:9 (after borrowing) -3 (from the subtrahend's ten thousands digit)=6\n\nHundred thousands place:8 (after borrowing) -1 (subtrahend's hundred thousands digit)=7\n\nMillions place:4 (from first number) -3 (subtrahend's millions digit)=1\n\nTen millions place:8 (from first number) -6 (subtrahend's ten millions digit)=2\n\nHundred millions place:7 (from first number) -9 (subtrahend's hundred millions digit). Wait, 7-9 can't do, so need to borrow from the billions place.\n\nThe billions place is 1. Borrow 1, making it 0, and add 10 to the hundred millions place, making it 17.\n\nNow, 17 -9=8.\n\nBillions place:0 (since we borrowed 1, but since it's the leading digit, we can omit it).\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nThe result of the subtraction is 781,767,453?\n\nWait, let's compile the digits:\n\nBillions place:0 (we can ignore).\n\nHundred millions:8\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:4\n\nTens:5\n\nUnits:3.\n\nWait, this is getting confusing. Let me write each digit step by step.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits:3\n\nTens:5\n\nHundreds:4\n\nThousands:7\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nMillions:1\n\nTen millions:2\n\nHundred millions:8\n\nBilli